  "slug": "japan-hfmd-hand-foot-and-mouth-disease-national-ca-e2de8cf0",
  "query": "Japan HFMD hand-foot-and-mouth disease national cases per sentinel (\u5b9a\u70b9\u5f53\u305f\u308a\u5831\u544a\u6570) Week 27 2026 provisional (\u901f\u5831) IDWR JIHS. Also confirmed Week 25 and Week 26 values, and week-over-week trajectory for weeks 20-27 of the 2026 season.",
  "answer": "I've completed the research on Japan's HFMD national sentinel surveillance for the 2026 season. Here's the summary:\n\n## Key findings\n\n**Week 27 2026 (provisional / \u901f\u5831)** \u2014 published by JIHS on 14 July 2026 (period 29 Jun \u2013 5 Jul):\n- **National cases per sentinel = 7.03** (15,845 total cases)\n- First time above the 5.0 alert threshold in ~2 years; 27 prefectures exceeded 5.0\n- 8th consecutive weekly increase\n\n**Confirmed prior weeks:**\n- **Week 25 (Jun 15\u201321): 3.40** per sentinel (7,576 cases)\n- **Week 26 (Jun 22\u201328): 4.61** per sentinel (10,396 cases)\n\n**Week-over-week trajectory (2026):**\n| Week | Per sentinel | WoW |\n|------|-------------|-----|\n| 20 | ~0.65 | start of rise |\n| 23 | 1.98 | \u2191 |\n| 24 | 2.75 | +39% |\n| 25 | 3.40 | +23.6% |\n| 26 | 4.61 | +35.6% |\n| 27 | 7.03 (prov.) | +52.5% |\n\nThe season shows steady, accelerating growth every week since Week 20 \u2014 characterized by JIHS as the largest HFMD outbreak since 2019/2020. It began in Kyushu, spread west, and reached the Tokyo metro area by weeks 25\u201326. Note that Week 27 is provisional and subject to revision; the next update was scheduled for 21 July 2026.\n\nThe confirmed Week 25 (3.40) and Week 26 (4.61) values come from JIHS-published IDWR data as reported by the pharmaceutical trade press (Jiho/\u65e5\u520a\u85ac\u696d), while Week 27 (7.03) is the provisional figure. Full sources and data points are recorded in the structured output.",
